  "claim_boundary": {
    "accepted": [
      "The fused boundary is implemented once across the Rust contract and CPU oracle, safe CUDA backend, checked bridge, handwritten CUDA, Stable ABI PyTorch dispatcher, and vLLM compiler adapter.",
      "The operator matches vLLM's compiled-native rounding boundary: SiLU and multiplication remain F32, then the product is rounded once to the input dtype before dynamic INT8 quantization.",
      "The real Qwen2.5 W8A8 graph replaces eligible SiLU-and-Mul-to-INT8 boundaries with Loom while both providers retain eight Cutlass scaled-mm call sites.",
      "Both provider orders match all 32 one-step top-1 tokens, all returned top-20 token sets, and every common logprob exactly.",
      "One ABI11 wheel containing exactly the Rust CUDA bridge and Stable ABI dispatcher passes fresh repository-free PyTorch 2.10/2.11 and vLLM 0.24/0.25 H20 gates.",
      "The provider remains disabled unless LOOM_KERNELS_ENABLE_SILU_AND_MUL_INT8 is explicitly enabled."
    ],
    "excluded": [
      "No stable end-to-end latency, TTFT, TPOT, throughput, or serving benefit is claimed.",
      "No CUDA Graph operator-boundary speedup is claimed; every measured rows-1-through-4096 ratio is below parity.",
      "Eager timing crosses unequal Python dispatcher boundaries and is diagnostic only.",
      "No GEMM implementation or GEMM speedup is claimed.",
      "The qualified ABI11 wheel is not published to a package index."
    ]
